<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Latest news from the Middle East, daily international news reports - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24’s coverage and analyses of political and social issues across the Middle East, including Egypt, the Gulf states, Iraq, Israel, Jordan, Lebanon, Saudi Arabia, Syria, Yemen and beyond.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/rss</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:07:51Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Who is Iran's 'influential spymaster' Hossein Taeb and does he pull the strings?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c000ce5bda7c01f1f4c39e4fe1687370a5bae9e3337e59a04e586ff10c9bc522</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:07:46Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T08:40:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20260914-who-is-iran-s-influential-spymaster-hossein-taeb-and-does-he-pull-the-strings--1568e0ad59bc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20260914-who-is-iran-s-influential-spymaster-hossein-taeb-and-does-he-pull-the-strings" /><summary type="html">PRESS REVIEW – Monday, September 14: The New York Times released an exclusive report titled “How Iran’s hard-liners prevailed and sabotaged the US peace deal”. Also: Trump says AI fears are "exaggerated", but reports show a different reality.</summary><category term="Press Review" /></entry><entry><title>Mideast live: Yemen’s Houthis say they targeted military facilities in Saudi Arabia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d50096c529ba4371750e2032477c72792ff09c06b0e06e81e473a9165761ed2a</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:07:48Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T03:39:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260914-middle-east-live-houthis-say-hit-saudi-base-after-renewed-fighting-with-yemeni-forces--2d4ac7dda5f0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260914-middle-east-live-houthis-say-hit-saudi-base-after-renewed-fighting-with-yemeni-forces" /><summary type="html">Yemen's Houthis on Monday said they fired dozens of drones and ballistic missiles at military targets in Saudi Arabia. The rebels have stepped up attacks on Saudi infrastructure while advancing along Yemen's Red Sea coast towards ​the Bab el-Mandeb Strait, a key shipping route. Follow our liveblog for the latest updates.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Iranian cargo vessel struck near Qeshm Island as Oman delays Tehran-Gulf talks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8ff459ed5eb89954faad1564e7d1d9443a638513dde91a9b36419734bb591a4c</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:07:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T02:35:36Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260914-iranian-ship-qeshm-island-tehran-hormuz--0939567a30d8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260914-iranian-ship-qeshm-island-tehran-hormuz" /><summary type="html">An Iranian cargo vessel was struck off Qeshm Island in the Strait of Hormuz on Sunday, killing one person and wounding four, Iranian state media said. Tehran blamed a “terrorist enemy” for the attack, which came as threats to shipping intensified around the Hormuz and Bab el-Mandeb straits.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Sucker Punch: How the Houthis shocked the Gulf</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fcb692bce94fb7f0368bf3fcee36703bbfa5b62942362f24a938984dc15f8d4c</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:05:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T18:46:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260913-sucker-punch-how-the-houthis-shocked-the-gulf--b9ad64708b93.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260913-sucker-punch-how-the-houthis-shocked-the-gulf" /><summary type="html">Who are the Houthis, what are their objectives for Yemen, and could the Iranian-backed group hold a significant part of world trade to ransom in the Bab el Mandeb Strait?
 
FRANCE 24’s Gavin Lee speaks with Professor Thomas Juneau, a specialist on the Houthis and Iran, explains the intricate dynamics of the group, its repressive nature and the level of the threat to world shipping.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Yemen: The Houthis test Iran's regional influence</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:edf02406fec6c37043363a20175cb69e5e89f013b351d87b8190eb07d18020f1</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:05:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T13:29:02Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260913-yemen-the-houthis-test-iran-s-regional-influence--7c06853f246c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260913-yemen-the-houthis-test-iran-s-regional-influence" /><summary type="html">Iran-backed Houthi attacks on Saudi Arabia have intensified as fighting spreads around the Bab el-Mandeb Strait, a vital chokepoint for global trade and oil shipments. On FRANCE 24, Sanaa Center for Strategic Studies chairman Farea Al-Muslimi argued this could mark "the last round in Yemen's current war", unpacking the Houthis' ties with Iran and the growing pressure on Washington as the group targets US allies while Donald Trump heads into a crucial election.</summary></entry><entry><title>Yemen: Fighting escalates around the Bab el-Mandeb Strait</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b5ac394a686e268b638860d37708452dd3fb8ac788aeb023b2bcfc67131f1125</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:05:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T13:15:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/yemen-fighting-escalates-around-the-bab-el-mandeb-strait--7a2aac2b3186.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/yemen-fighting-escalates-around-the-bab-el-mandeb-strait" /><summary type="html">Fighting is escalating in Yemen after Iran-backed Houthi forces seized strategic territory around the Bab el-Mandeb Strait, prompting counterstrikes by government forces and reported Saudi air raids. The Houthis also claimed attacks inside southern Saudi Arabia and threatened to disrupt shipping through the key maritime chokepoint, raising fears for regional security and global trade.</summary></entry><entry><title>Yemen: Houthi offensive triggers new displacement crisis</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:199f0bb010ebf28e74cc9e38a0fbaf161f5e675099d3d7ad86a9a765aa070fa0</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:05:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T09:18:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/yemen-houthi-offensive-triggers-new-displacement-crisis--2ca71fdc0d39.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/yemen-houthi-offensive-triggers-new-displacement-crisis" /><summary type="html">More than 70,000 people have fled their homes in Yemen after Iran-backed Houthi rebels launched an offensive to seize the Bab el-Mandeb Strait, with many escaping to Aden and around 1,400 crossing into neighbouring Djibouti. The UN and IOM warn the new displacement wave is worsening an already dire humanitarian crisis in a country devastated by 12 years of war.</summary></entry><entry><title>Houthis say hit Saudi base amid renewed fighting with Yemeni forces</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:97540d0a96da96eb3c9cc5ea0064da8147942f0695f86a0f35de56dc9af3414d</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:05:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T05:11:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260913-middle-east-live-houthis-say-hit-saudi-base-after-renewed-fighting-with-yemeni-forces--80232e475ad4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260913-middle-east-live-houthis-say-hit-saudi-base-after-renewed-fighting-with-yemeni-forces" /><summary type="html">Yemeni Houthi rebels claimed responsibility on Sunday for an attack on a military base in southern Saudi Arabia as renewed fighting with Yemen's government forces forced growing numbers of civilians to flee. Fighting in western Yemen over the past few weeks has left hundreds dead and displaced tens of thousands of people. Read our blog to see how the day's events unfolded.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Saudi Arabia closes East-West pipeline as Houthis tighten grip on Red Sea</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e10c2d859f6e377cf000e5e5453d6188917c74ca71675ff23f197469e374f1f2</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:05:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T20:51:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260912-saudi-arabia-shut-down-east-west-pipeline-as-houthis-tighten-grip-on-red-sea--806e159c0921.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260912-saudi-arabia-shut-down-east-west-pipeline-as-houthis-tighten-grip-on-red-sea" /><summary type="html">Saudi Arabia on Saturday ​shut down the vital East-West pipeline after the conduit came under attack in the widening Middle East war, threatening to send energy prices soaring. The 1,200-km pipeline has served as the main route out for global ​supplies of Middle East oil for the ‌past six months while the Strait of Hormuz has been largely shut by war.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Has Trump Left MBS hanging over Yemen?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1c35fe4ce1209864d96d3c28738843373cb95b4550a88bde9747d5755a298a7e</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:05:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T18:49:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260912-has-trump-left-mbs-hanging-over-yemen--36647a88beb9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260912-has-trump-left-mbs-hanging-over-yemen" /><summary type="html">The Yemeni and Saudi governments are under pressure. The Saudi Crown Prince Mohammed Bin Salman reportedly called US President Donald Trump twice to ask him to authorise US strikes against the Houthis in Yemen over the threat to the Bab el Mandeb Strait. According to Axios, the US President declined. FRANCE 24’s Gavin Lee discusses that decision and the wider conflict with  the retired Lieutenant General Ben Hodges, former commander of US ground forces in Europe, and former Commander of NATO Allied Land Command in Izmir, Turkey.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Jewish ‘supercop’ runs on Arab ticket in Israeli polls – and sparks a storm</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bd4d4595e9c88e7cfe4d6cd6f1a95c790c7887a7fc67655bb64be2ad28315410</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:05:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T09:50:28Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260912-jewish-supercop-runs-on-arab-ticket-in-israeli-polls-_-and-sparks-a-storm--26e2eab65f03.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260912-jewish-supercop-runs-on-arab-ticket-in-israeli-polls-%E2%80%93-and-sparks-a-storm" /><summary type="html">Former Israeli police officer Yoav Segalovitz's decision to run as the No. 2 candidate on the Arab Raam party ticket in the October 2026 elections marks a paradigm change in Israeli politics. Far-right politicians have slammed the move, but it could pave the way for an Arab party to join a coalition opposing Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu and his allies.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Iran got Chinese satellite images before deadly strike on US troops, report reveals</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:01f29e24658ee603696c4d3e5ce3e9eae972b5a7655e43249d2b51f726e25d1f</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:05:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T05:19:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260912-live-saudi-arabia-oil-pipeline-shut-down-after-drone-attack-launched-from-iraq--7ddf3d05e286.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260912-live-saudi-arabia-oil-pipeline-shut-down-after-drone-attack-launched-from-iraq" /><summary type="html">A report released by The Wall Street Journal on Saturday said Chinese entities supplied Iran with satellite images of a base in Jordan before and after an attack that killed three US soldiers. US President Donald Trump has warned Beijing not to sell weapons to Iran, and in May, Washington sanctioned three China-based satellite firms for enabling Iran's military operations.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Iran-backed Houthis seize near control of vital Bab el-Mandeb shipping lane</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:463d6e4eae3776ba69b495e9c0970eb80eae5855d7bb1f5945410716a658ddf6</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:05:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T20:09:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260911-iran-backed-houthis-seize-near-control-of-vital-bab-el-mandeb-shipping-lane--31b17fb442d1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260911-iran-backed-houthis-seize-near-control-of-vital-bab-el-mandeb-shipping-lane" /><summary type="html">Yemen's Iran-aligned Houthi rebels captured the strategic Perim Island in the Bab el-Mandeb Strait, located at the southern entrance to the Red Sea, officials said on Friday. The lightning move opens a new front in the Iran war and threatens energy supplies, especially Saudi oil exports, from passing through one of the world's key shipping lanes.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Lebanon: Tremor recorded as Israel says destroyed key Hezbollah tunnels</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e109273987840daa1ccad0f0e8a8033e186fb4de44514ecca8f47047b7382b20</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:05:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T14:14:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260911-lebanon-tremor-recorded-as-israel-says-destroyed-key-hezbollah-tunnels--dcbda6b6879f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260911-lebanon-tremor-recorded-as-israel-says-destroyed-key-hezbollah-tunnels" /><summary type="html">Israel said Thursday it demolished key tunnels built by the Iran-backed Hezbollah group beneath the strategic Ali al-Taher ridge in southern Lebanon, triggering a 4.1-magnitude tremor.</summary></entry><entry><title>Houthis seize entire Red Sea coast of Yemen</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9ff9f1c47937a9add270a6777d9c4a27e8163a0bcdde4101ce34b24df50e6626</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:05:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T04:52:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260911-middle-east-live-trump-says-he-has-no-regrets-about-launching-war-on-iran--68a101e1037f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260911-middle-east-live-trump-says-he-has-no-regrets-about-launching-war-on-iran" /><summary type="html">Yemen's Iran-aligned Houthi rebels have seized control of the country's entire Red Sea coast, a government official said on Friday. The move inches the rebels closer to gaining near total control of the Bab al-Mandab strait, a vital shipping corridor. Read about the day’s events as they unfolded on our liveblog.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Yemen's Iran-backed Houthi rebels seize strategic Red Sea port city of Mocha</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bf8c7df93122b35c71406882d258b1c6d2a5089a50d9c1768d0815ff59614472</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:05:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T22:55:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260910-yemen-houthis-city-red-sea-iran--0d8343d16cb2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260910-yemen-houthis-city-red-sea-iran" /><summary type="html">Yemen’s Houthis seized the strategic Red Sea port city of Mocha on Thursday as their offensive against Saudi-backed government forces intensified. Saudi Arabia launched dozens of airstrikes over the past 24 hours, the Houthis said, after the Iran-backed group carried out attacks on Saudi territory that wounded dozens of people.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Israel destroys Hezbollah tunnel network in south Lebanon, triggering 4.1-magnitude tremor</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2a6bb9b3593391227f5f6eecabdf2d56d51fe2387d7fcb1200be9a995f2000cb</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:05:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T21:50:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260910-israel-hezbollah-tunnels-lebanon-earthquake--c28ae45e8d7b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260910-israel-hezbollah-tunnels-lebanon-earthquake" /><summary type="html">Israel said on Thursday it destroyed key tunnels built by Iran-backed Hezbollah beneath the strategic Ali al-Taher ridge in southern Lebanon, completing what it called operational control of the area. Lebanon reported a massive explosion, while the US Geological Survey recorded a magnitude 4.1 tremor nearby.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Iran-backed Houthi rebels take strategic port city in Yemen, raising threat to Red Sea shipping</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0633baeda9a328df2f0506df4b10a3238a22ab2d29a9109ea2712f052ae27bf2</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:05:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T19:18:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/iran-backed-houthi-rebels-take-strategic-port-city-in-yemen-raising-threat-to-red-sea-shipping--ea40bb9d282d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/iran-backed-houthi-rebels-take-strategic-port-city-in-yemen-raising-threat-to-red-sea-shipping" /><summary type="html">The Iran-backed Houthi rebel group on Thursday took over Yemen’s port city of Mokha, an area vital to controlling shipping through the Red Sea, Houthi and Yemeni officials said. Mokha is about 80 kilometers (50 miles) from the Bab el-Mandeb Strait, a waterway that connects the Red Sea and the Gulf of Aden and through which about 12% of the world’s goods are typically shipped. FRANCE 24's Nick Rushworth reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Iran raises fuel prices for heavy users</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5357c664e52483905c5bd9cd9385266a61ff52afcd5e0f493a3ef0e9109da0cf</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:05:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T18:48:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/iran-raises-fuel-prices-for-heavy-users--e0de25d0e71c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/iran-raises-fuel-prices-for-heavy-users" /><summary type="html">The rise of the price of fuel is an issue for both the United States and Iran in this conflict. US president Donald Trump has conceded that prices will not fall before the midterm elections where the US voters could hold him to account. Meanwhile in Iran where many communities have been bombed since February 28th, there's now the added problem of incresing fuel prices. FRANCE 24's Ali al Basha sent this report.</summary></entry><entry><title>Israeli-made film about use of AI for mass killing in Gaza gets record ovation at Venice premiere</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bdb02013af8850a5c503c7585833725bd717c7cf6b250bc46b442271edb37fc7</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:05:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T18:19:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260910-israeli-made-film-about-mass-killings-in-gaza-gets-25-minute-ovation-at-venice-premiere--b2af8e05ac00.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260910-israeli-made-film-about-mass-killings-in-gaza-gets-25-minute-ovation-at-venice-premiere" /><summary type="html">A film documenting Israel's use of artificial intelligence to facilitate the mass killing of Palestinian civilians in the Gaza Strip received a record 25-minute standing ovation at the Venice Film Festival on Thursday. "NAZA" details the brutal Israeli bombardment of the Palestinian territory through anonymous interviews with two dozen whistleblowers from the Israeli military or intelligence services.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>‘I’m spending my savings just to survive’: Iran’s economic crisis fuels new protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7de2f73761cf2f95daf2a094d13d906009a407237144aa1206030abdfdf92e79</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:05:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T14:30:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260910-iran-economic-crisis-protests-war-repression--4c3dfe4a3dc9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260910-iran-economic-crisis-protests-war-repression" /><summary type="html">Despite severe security risks and an ongoing war, retirees, nurses, workers, teachers and students have held sit-ins and protests across Iran since this summer, most often over economic hardship. With prices going up every few hours, salaries and pensions going unpaid for months, and unemployment increasing, our Observers say life is becoming “impossible”.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Netanyahu visits troops in occupied Syria as Damascus slams 'blatant violation' of sovereignty</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5e0ea0794324217d20a6815563f8489fe43cfd182f223953cb7e15855ccd080d</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:05:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T06:23:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260910-netanyahu-visits-troops-occupied-syria-damascus-slams-blatant-violation-sovereignty--d21e5845a5ed.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260910-netanyahu-visits-troops-occupied-syria-damascus-slams-blatant-violation-sovereignty" /><summary type="html">Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu made a third visit to Israeli troops in an occupied stretch of Syria Wednesday, sparking fresh condemnation from Damascus. Netanyahu repeated his claim that the Iranian government is on the verge of collapse as the US-Israeli war against Iran drags on.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Oil spike past $100 dampens stock prices, fans inflation fears</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c3527c8d4a560195d30ea930022b53c438f9eed2dad90767a78504fa53e63e20</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:05:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T02:47:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260910-stock-prices-drop-as-oil-spike-fans-fears-of-worsening-inflation--87326a3a1a8d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260910-stock-prices-drop-as-oil-spike-fans-fears-of-worsening-inflation" /><summary type="html">As the US and Iran trade air strikes in the vital Strait of Hormuz and Yemen's Houthi rebels step up their campaign against Saudi Arabia, surging oil prices have seen stocks falling across Asia. Investors appear to be holding their breath for the news that the Federal Reserve and other central banks will raise interest rates to tamp down the expected inflation.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Houthis close in on Bab el-Mandeb as Brent barrel price soars to over $106</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7f67151bfdfd19d3d5c6e6619819b06eaaa3ad92cc2df23287bf75a54a4ab25f</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:05:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T02:46:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260910-middle-east-live-trump-warns-iran-not-to-get-cute-over-activity-at-pickaxe-mountain--16e2d74b863a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260910-middle-east-live-trump-warns-iran-not-to-get-cute-over-activity-at-pickaxe-mountain" /><summary type="html">Yemen's Iran-aligned Houthis on Thursday gained further leverage over the Bab el-Mandeb Strait, one of the world's most critical shipping routes amid the ongoing blockade of the Strait of Hormuz. Meanwhile, price for Brent crude oil soared more than 5 percent to over $106 per barrel. Read our blog to see how the day's events unfolded.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Iran and US strike tankers in biggest shipping attack since war began</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0b79619edce8e483a807870fe0e89efeadd85d5b67f8ff14e33b57ffc76ed70d</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:05:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T20:31:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260909-iran-and-us-strike-tankers-in-biggest-shipping-attack-since-war-began--4d2b3cd0d7d2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260909-iran-and-us-strike-tankers-in-biggest-shipping-attack-since-war-began" /><summary type="html">Iran and the US on Wednesday traded their biggest wave of attacks on shipping since the war began, with Iran saying it struck 10 vessels near the Strait of Hormuz after US forces sank five Iranian oil tankers. Brent crude oil surged above $100 a barrel as fears grew over global energy supplies.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Houthi offensive on Bab al-Mandeb may bring 'tremendous leverage', analyst explains</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5de9d4239a4e4381ae990dda873b84974238492f357639f942a971fd76cb4592</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:05:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T19:35:36Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/houthi-offensive-on-bab-al-mandeb-may-bring-tremendous-leverage-analyst-explains--fe459ea32af6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/houthi-offensive-on-bab-al-mandeb-may-bring-tremendous-leverage-analyst-explains" /><summary type="html">The Saudi-led coalition in Yemen on Wednesday said the Iran-backed Houthis had launched fresh attacks on the kingdom's south, after the rebels launched an offensive seeking to control the Bab al-Mandab Strait. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Mark Owen, Adam Baron, Fellow at the New America Foundation, says that "if you have both groups able to disrupt maritime shipping both in the Red Sea and the Gulf, this would be a tremendous exercise of leverage to put pressure for a resolution".</summary></entry><entry><title>Iran strikes ships, expands no-go zone outside Hormuz strait</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5dcdfb1623a1e982758811557c82750729152ad2c20ae164fdf74c4c7436b94c</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:05:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T18:30:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/iran-strikes-ships-expands-no-go-zone-outside-hormuz-strait--ad14b4ac2e24.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/iran-strikes-ships-expands-no-go-zone-outside-hormuz-strait" /><summary type="html">Iran said it attacked more than a dozen vessels trying to pass through the Strait of Hormuz on Wednesday, as it announced an expansion of a no-go zone outside the strategic waterway it has blockaded for months. The fresh attacks and fighting with the United States have sent oil prices above $100 per barrel again as Tehran chokes off the strait and Washington presses a counter-blockade of Iranian ports. FRANCE 24's Reza Sayah reports from Tehran.</summary></entry><entry><title>The Times: 'Counterproductive' sanctions on Israel don't match the 'theatrical rhetoric'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a1a8caa61c58c81c11ba28d56fb4c64051cc6ab3be852bf083df9f3a4dd8bfc0</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:05:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T13:35:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20260909-the-times-counterproductive-sanctions-on-israel-don-t-match-the-theatrical-rhetoric--24a57d7cc6c6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20260909-the-times-counterproductive-sanctions-on-israel-don-t-match-the-theatrical-rhetoric" /><summary type="html">PRESS REVIEW – Wednesday, September 9: British papers are reacting to the sanctions imposed on Israel. Next: Israeli papers discuss Haaretz's October 7 revelatory investigation. Also: CDs are back! Finally, South Park renames itself to South America to mock Trump.</summary><category term="Press Review" /></entry><entry><title>'New escalation in Yemen deeply concerning everyone in the region'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:265305d68450518a70f2bda8f8fdacf54cbe344f5d7835911d3d77a25c77f8ab</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:05:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T10:39:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/new-escalation-in-yemen-deeply-concerning-everyone-in-the-region--833547815e7f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/new-escalation-in-yemen-deeply-concerning-everyone-in-the-region" /><summary type="html">Oliver Farry is pleased to welcome Jules Grange Gastinel, Researcher at the Institute for Research and Studies on the Arab and Muslim World (IREMAM). He depicts Yemen as moving from a prolonged condition of unresolved conflict into renewed regional confrontation. The relative calm established after 2022, he argues, never amounted to a durable political settlement: Yemen remains divided between rival political, financial and military institutions.</summary></entry></feed>
